    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`. Verified example from the run: `NSW2716E6609E1` = `NSW` + `27` (FY) + `16E6609E` (HASH8) + `1` (CHK).\n\n**Identity generation**\n- Renamed `AssignCustomerCode` \u2192 `AssignMemberId`. It now builds `REGION` (from postcode) + `FY` (2-digit fiscal year of the business-day-adjusted registrationDate) + `HASH8` (first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over telephone+lastName) + `CHK` (Luhn over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`, computed inline). Collision handling now de-duplicates the whole `memberId` by appending `-<n>`.\n- Updated `owners.POST.yml` step name and class reference.\n\n**Model & persistence**\n- `Owner`: field/column `customerCode`/`customer_code` \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id`, accessors `getMemberId`/`setMemberId`; `getPrimaryIdentifier()` now returns the memberId. Renamed the column in all four `schema.sql` files (widened to `VARCHAR(32)` / `TEXT`).\n\n**DTO derivation (`OwnerMapper` + helpers)**\n- Removed the `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` mappings; deleted the now-unused `CheckDigit` helper. `memberId` auto-maps by name.\n- `Locality` now extracts the region as the leading prefix of the dash-free memberId (matching `NSW`/`VIC`/`QLD`, else `UNKNOWN`); `ownerSegment` and `timezone` follow it.\n- The standalone `fiscalYear` now **references the memberId** \u2014 derived from its FY segment via a new `MemberId.fiscalYear(...)` helper \u2014 rather than being recomputed from the registrationDate.\n\n**Audit record**\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent` field/JSON key `customerCode` \u2192 `memberId`; `AuditOwnerCreated` logs `memberId` and drops the removed fields.\n\n**API contract**\n- `openapi.yml`: replaced the `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`/`checkDigit` schema properties with `memberId`, and updated the `fiscalYear` and `locality` descriptions.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the spec said \"the fiscal-year value ... must reference the memberId,\" so I made the DTO's `fiscalYear` extract the FY segment out of the memberId. For any created owner this is identical to the old registrationDate-derived value, so it's behavior-preserving there; it only differs for records with no assigned memberId (e.g. seed data), where it now yields `null` \u2014 no test exercises that path.",
